                                "example_id": "f4177001-6d57-41aa-a1e0-9cb343516c32",
                                "sense_id": "6152959f-ce14-32fd-86a8-671d81b7d983",
                                "text": "For instance, it was described in 1941 how a solution of the enzyme pepsin could be used to remove gelatine from the expensive part of the lacquer record, the even and flat metal blank, and how to cook new gelatine and how to dip-coat the cleaned blank."
                            },
